  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing water security challenges through scientific cooperation, innovation and institutional capacities strengthening in the Gulf region &amp; Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gulf region is geographically one of the hottest and most water scarce region in the world. The lack of freshwater in the region is exacerbated by high rates of population growth, accelerated economic development and industrialization, inadequate water resources management, vulnerability to climate change, declining water quality and accessibility constraints due to conflicts and instability. The objective of this workplan is to assist member states in the Gulf region &amp; Yemen to address water scarcity challenges through mobilizing cooperation and strengthening the role of research in water sciences to respond the region&#x2019;s needs to achieve water security. The workplan will directly contribute to the IHP IX Operational Plan 2022-2029.</narrative>
  </description>
